# Baseline content that ships in every Player package, relative to Assets/.
# Build > Package Project starts with this list and adds the selected startup
# Scene plus its texture, model/material and skybox dependency closure.
#
# DECLARED, not discovered. The staging step used to copy Assets\ wholesale,
# which made the package a function of whatever happened to sit in a
# developer's working folder rather than of the commit:
#
#   - 51 of the package's 51.6 MB were files git does not track, so a fresh
#     clone of the SAME commit produced a completely different package while
#     package-manifest.txt still claimed commit=... source_state=clean.
#   - laevat\ (43 MB) was gitignored in 11.2.5 precisely because it is
#     third-party art that cannot be redistributed - and the packaging step
#     copied it straight into the thing meant for redistribution. No shipped
#     Scene even references it.
#
# Adding an asset here is therefore a deliberate act. Omitting one that a
# shipped Scene needs is caught at package time, not by a user: staging fails
# on an entry that matches nothing, and VerifyPlayerPackage.ps1 then RUNS both
# Scenes outside the repository, where a missing texture surfaces as a failed
# load rather than a silent fallback.
#
# Entries may be literal paths or wildcards. Blank lines and #-comments are
# ignored. Every staged file must also be tracked by git, so that the commit
# recorded in the manifest is genuinely enough to rebuild this package.

# --- Scenes the package can start with ---
# Demo.scene is the default; ShadowA.scene is what VerifyPlayerPackage.ps1
# passes through --scene, so the explicit-Scene path is exercised too.
Scenes/Demo.scene
Scenes/ShadowA.scene

# --- textures the two Scenes name ---
Crate.png
Floor.png
TestNormal.png

# --- the skybox Demo.scene names ---
# A cube map is six files under one logical name; all six or none.
Skyboxes/Test/px.png
Skyboxes/Test/nx.png
Skyboxes/Test/py.png
Skyboxes/Test/ny.png
Skyboxes/Test/pz.png
Skyboxes/Test/nz.png
